implementationPlan.description:
MERGE DUPLICATE gotcha-* AND decision-* MEMORIES. Read only the candidate groups, never all 379 files.

Candidates:
(a) Name clusters: hyphen tokens after the gotcha-/decision- prefix, stopwords dropped, plural 's'/'es' stripped, Jaccard >= 0.5 with at least 2 shared tokens, union-find.
(b) Seed topic groups:
- contested landing: gotcha-contested-path-dropped-unless-tool-tier, gotcha-contested-path-never-lands, gotcha-contested-path-silently-skipped-from-landing, gotcha-contested-path-needs-edit-tool-to-land, gotcha-contested-path-skipped-overlay-gate-false-green;
- shared-file sweeps: gotcha-shared-file-hunks-land-under-first-committer, gotcha-landing-peer-sweeps-shared-doc-hunks;
- plan-text rails: gotcha-submit-plan-rails-scan-plan-text, gotcha-submit-plan-rail-scan-and-unlanded-files, gotcha-moe-rails-grep-plan-text, decision-plan-text-rails;
- vscode harness: gotcha-vscode-tests, gotcha-vscode-vm-test-harness, gotcha-vscode-vm-test-harnesses, gotcha-vscode-vm-test-realm-artifacts;
- the gotcha-local-runner-*tests* files;
- gotcha-daemon-dead-mcp-connect-timeout + gotcha-moe-mcp-connect-timeout-dead-daemon;
- gotcha-agent-session-env-leaks-into-tests + gotcha-seat-env-leaks-into-daemon-tests;
- gotcha-codex-worker-tui-skips-wrapper-postflight + gotcha-interactive-tui-skips-wrapper-postflight;
- gotcha-cq-plan-size-vs-qa-cap + gotcha-qa-size-cap-inconsistency-cq-v;
- gotcha-get-context-shape-and-fallback + gotcha-get-context-unrecorded-shape-unpinned.

For each group:
- Merge only true duplicates or near-duplicates (same subject, overlapping facts).
- Complementary rows stay separate, with a one-line reason. Examples: the per-task decision-cq-*-split rows; decision-protected-runtime-selection vs -confirmations.

Merging:
- Keep the most general existing name, or a docs/MEMORY.md-style topic name.
- The kept file must carry EVERY distinct fact, with dates and task ids kept as provenance. Write it with Serena write_memory or edit_memory.
- Move the merged-away files to _archive/ the same way as in step 2.
- Then grep the live (non-_archive) memories for `mem:<merged-away>` and bare `<merged-away>` references and re-point them to the kept name.
- References inside .moe task plans are NOT edited: list them (read-only grep) for the summary.

Record each merge as 'kept <name> <- merged <names>'.

Error handling: if a fact's merge is ambiguous, keep both bullets verbatim. Never drop a fact to shorten.
